<title>FRANCE: Oddo adds Alcatel to list, drops Pinault.</title>
<headline>Oddo adds Alcatel to list, drops Pinault.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage house Oddo said on Wednesday that it had dropped retail conglomerate Pinault-Printemps-Redoute from its favoured list and replaced it with electrical engineering firm Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>It cited the improvement forecast for Alcatel's telecoms operating margin in last week's preliminary results, boosting its target for the share to between 630 and 710 francs.</p>
<p>It dropped Pinault-Printemps from the list after its shares attained the target of 2,300 francs and also lowered its recommendation on the stock to overweight from buy.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
